 "findings": {
  "1_campaign_policy": "decision_policy \"required\" refuses a config (LoadConfig) unless the ladder is exactly director +0 s, duty +300 s, external rung +600 s with absolute command, absolute ledger + kind, absolute resolve_cmd, and responders. Structural checks always (one of seat/exec, known seat, absolute paths, order, window 0..86400). Generic default unchanged (director, duty +300). Prospective campaign4 config: plans/campaign4-decision-config.prospective.json (NOT installed; its resolve_cmd names ~/.config/agent-deck/escalation-resolve, which exists only after a signed promotion). Tests: omitted, malformed (10 variants), full; LoadConfig refusal.",
  "2_3_exec_retry_and_ambiguity": "Attempts[rung] persisted BEFORE each effect; at most 2 transport attempts per rung and per re-raise, 30 s apart; then 'unresolved' in status plus ONE director notice (D3 key decision|incident|k|unresolved). Reopen keeps the count. An uncertain attempt ('intended', crash before the outcome) with a durable ledger record of the key since then is recorded sent with that receipt and not re-sent; seat rungs keep the D3 labelled repeat. Failure is never an acknowledgement.",
  "4_responder_identity": "decision-ack needs --cap-file: 256-bit random secret per incident and responder, file mode 0600 in <db>.caps (0700), the notice names the path only, the loop stores sha256 + expiry (15 min) only, rotated on every external send (re-raise makes the old secret stale). Refused: literal claude without proof, guessed, wrong, stale, expired, other incident's, withdrawn responder, deadline > 15 min. TRUST BOUNDARY: any process of the same Unix user can read the file; this is not adversarial isolation. No secret in argv, notice, ledger, status, claim, git (witness grep: no leak).",
  "5_watcher_resolution": "PRIVATE adapters/escalation-watch (installed copy + resolved()) and adapters/escalation-resolve (append-only {t, ack:R-<incident>, resolve:KEY, incident, by, note}; the 'ack' field keeps the installed escalations tool and watcher working on such a record). A decision writes ONE resolution record per key; records of that key at/before it do not page; a later record pages; an ack alone never resolves. watch_test.sh 22/22: 5 non-P13 ledgers give identical output, pages and state vs the installed watcher. Installed watcher/timer/config/production ledger untouched.",
  "6_mutants": "176 of 176 caught on 6a44c76 (parallel 4 workers, per-mutant logs mutlogs-final/). First run on df5e6fc: 175/176, the survivor 'any principal may acknowledge' killed by a new test (withdrawn responder). The 2 initial survivors, 2 invalid and 2 unapplied were re-anchored and are caught; 12 new mutants. Serial/parallel equivalence: identical (cmp): 9 of 9 Go mutants caught"
 },
